---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/page/PageHero.astro';
import Band from '../components/ui/Band.astro';
import Prose from '../components/page/Prose.astro';
import { staticRow, org, editorialFor } from '../lib/page.js';
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/site.js';

const ed = editorialFor('privacy');
const row = staticRow({
  path: '/privacy',
  pageType: 'core',
  title: ed.metaTitle ?? 'Privacy Policy | MrMoverPacker',
  h1: ed.title ?? 'Privacy policy',
  metaDescription:
    ed.seoDescription ??
    'How MrMoverPacker collects, uses, shares and protects your personal data, and your rights under India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.',
  breadcrumbs: [{ path: '/', anchor: 'Home' }],
});
const o = org();
const legalName = o?.legalName ?? 'MR MOVER PACKER';
const brand = o?.brandName ?? 'MrMoverPacker';
---

<BaseLayout row={row}>
  <PageHero
    dark
    eyebrow={ed.eyebrow ?? 'Legal'}
    h1={row.h1}
    intro={ed.intro ??
      'What we collect, why we collect it, and the control you have over it, written to India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and in language you can actually follow.'}
    breadcrumbs={row.breadcrumbs}
    current="Privacy"
  />

  <Band label="Privacy">
    <Prose>
      {
        ed.bodyHtml ? (
          <Fragment set:html={ed.bodyHtml} />
        ) : (
          <Fragment>
            <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 17 October 2026</p>

            <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
            <p>
              This policy explains how <strong>{legalName}</strong>, trading as {brand} ("we",
              "us"), handles your personal data when you use this website or move with us. We decide
              why and how your data is used, which makes us the data fiduciary under India's Digital
              Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.
            </p>

            <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>What you give us:</strong> your name, phone number, email, pickup and drop
                addresses, move date and details, and any photos or video of your home you share for
                a survey. For a car or bike move, the vehicle details and a copy of its RC and
                insurance.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>If you create an account:</strong> your name, mobile number and city, and,
                if you add them, your email and saved addresses (with the floor and whether there is
                a lift), plus when you last signed in. Your password is stored only in scrambled
                (hashed) form, so nobody at {brand}, our staff included, can read it.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>During your move:</strong> the photo inventory, signatures at pickup and
                delivery, your coordinator's notes, and records of calls and WhatsApp messages with
                us.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Payments:</strong> the amount, date and payment reference. We do not store
                card numbers or banking passwords.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>From your device:</strong> pages visited, the device and browser used, a
                rough location from your IP address, and cookies (section 7).
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>To send you an estimate, survey your goods and prepare your written quote.</li>
              <li>To plan and carry out your move, and keep you updated on the day.</li>
              <li>
                To run your account: let you sign in, show your quotes and moves in one place, and
                keep your saved addresses ready for your next quote. Once we have confirmed your
                mobile number with you, earlier quote requests from that number appear in your
                account too.
              </li>
              <li>To handle claims, complaints and questions.</li>
              <li>To issue GST invoices and meet our legal, tax and accounting duties.</li>
              <li>To keep the website and our records secure and prevent fraud.</li>
              <li>
                To understand how the website is used and how our advertising performs, so we can
                improve both.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              We use your data on the basis of your consent, which you give when you send us a form
              or contact us, and for the uses the law allows without it, such as meeting tax and
              legal duties. You can withdraw consent at any time (section 6); this does not affect
              what was done before.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Our crew and coordinators,</strong> who see the details they need for your
                move: your name, phone number, addresses and inventory.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Service providers</strong> who run our website, hosting, email, messaging
                and records for us, under contract and only to do that work.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Google</strong>, through Google Analytics, which tells us how the website is
                used.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Meta (Facebook)</strong>, through the Meta pixel, which tells us whether our
                ads lead to quote requests. When you send a quote request, your phone number and
                email may be shared with Meta in hashed (scrambled) form to match it to an ad. Meta
                cannot read them from the hash.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Payment and banking partners</strong>, to process what you pay us.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>For transit insurance,</strong> only if you choose it: the details needed to
                issue the policy and handle a claim.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Authorities</strong>, when the law requires it or to protect someone's
                safety.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              <strong>We do not sell your personal data.</strong>
            </p>

            <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
            <p>
              We keep your data only as long as we need it for the purposes above. Invoices and the
              records behind them are kept for as long as tax and accounting law requires. After
              that, data is deleted or anonymised.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you have an account, we keep it until you ask us to close it. When we close it, we
              delete your account details and saved addresses; records of a move that the law
              requires us to keep, or that a claim depends on, are kept for as long as that applies.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
            <p>Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask us to:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Tell you what personal data we hold about you and how we use it.</li>
              <li>Correct, complete or update it.</li>
              <li>
                Erase it, where we no longer need it and the law does not require us to keep it.
              </li>
              <li>Stop using it, by withdrawing your consent.</li>
              <li>Close your account and delete its details.</li>
              <li>Let someone you nominate exercise these rights for you.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=Privacy`}>{EMAIL}</a> with "Privacy" in the
              subject. We reply within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can
              complain to the Data Protection Board of India. If you have an account, you can also
              see and change most of your details yourself on your account page.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
            <p>
              The website uses cookies to work properly, and analytics and advertising cookies from
              Google Analytics and the Meta pixel (section 4). If you sign in to your account, two
              cookies keep you signed in for up to 30 days: one holds your sign-in and cannot be
              read by the page's scripts, the other holds your first name so the page can greet you.
              Signing out removes both. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings;
              the website still works without them, except that you cannot stay signed in. You can
              also use Google's Analytics opt-out browser add-on and your Facebook ad settings.
            </p>

            <h2>8. How we protect it</h2>
            <p>
              We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards, limit who can see your data
              to the people who need it, and collect only what we need. Account passwords are
              scrambled one way before they are stored, signing in is paused for 15 minutes after
              five wrong passwords, and only our administrators can see account records. If you
              forget your password, we set a new one and send it only to the mobile number on your
              account. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects you, we will tell you and
              the authorities as the law requires.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Children</h2>
            <p>
              Our services are for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone
              under 18.
            </p>

            <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>
              We may update this policy as our practices or the law change. The date at the top
              shows when it last changed.
            </p>

            <h2>11. Contact</h2>
            <p>
              Questions about your data? Email{' '}
              <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=Privacy`}>{EMAIL}</a> or reach us through the{' '}
              <a href="/company/contact">contact page</a>.
            </p>
          </Fragment>
        )
      }
    </Prose>
  </Band>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-updated {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
  }
</style>
